; ======================================================================
;  hw_gnss.pi4 - the HwGnss* seam (Anvil/Hal/hal.pbi) on the Pi 4 and 5.
;
;  Phase A item 2b. The receiver is reached through Anvil/Services/gnss.pbi,
;  which reads it from a source - USB today (Lib/usbserial.pi4: CDC-ACM and
;  the four bridge chips GNSS Bridge accepts), Bluetooth, Bluetooth LE and
;  the network as named placeholders - and frames and decodes its stream
;  the way the GNSS Bridge Pico does.
;
;  HwGnssUp() opens the source set at the prompt (gnss.source: USB unless
;  `gnss source network` set the network). Choosing another source is GnssOpen(src); the
;  placeholders answer with a sentence (HwGnssErrText) rather than nothing.
;  There is no PPS input wired on this board, so HwGnssPpsTicks() is -1.
; ======================================================================

; The source set at the prompt (the setting gnss.source: usb, the default, or network); see gnss_cmd.pbi.
Procedure.i HwGnssUp()
  Define *p
  If GnssSource() <> #GNSS_SRC_NONE
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  *p = SettingsGet("gnss.source")
  If *p <> 0
    If PeekA(*p) = 110 And PeekA(*p + 1) = 101 And PeekA(*p + 2) = 116            ; "net..."
      ProcedureReturn GnssOpen(#GNSS_SRC_NETWORK)
    EndIf
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn GnssOpen(#GNSS_SRC_USB)
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwGnssPoll()
  ProcedureReturn GnssPump()
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwGnssFix(*fix)
  ProcedureReturn GnssFix(*fix)
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwGnssAgeMs()
  ProcedureReturn GnssAgeMs()
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwGnssPpsTicks()
  ProcedureReturn -1
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwGnssSatsUsed()
  ProcedureReturn GnssSatsUsed()
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwGnssErrText()
  ProcedureReturn GnssWhy()
EndProcedure
